Subject: [PATCH 15/20] =?UTF-8?q?hw/arm:=20flintstone=20board=20companion?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20the=20button=20and=20the=20board=20lines=20over?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20a=20chardev?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The physical product around the SoC, as a chardev so something outside
QEMU can press the button and watch what the firmware drives, with
nothing in the guest knowing it is watched:

  HU-BUTTON   out of this device, into GPIO2_IO18 — the gpio-keys "HU
              Button" (active high, KEY_ENTER). set/hold/dump over the
              chardev, hold timed in guest time so long presses survive
              -icount.
  POWEROFF    GPIO1_IO11 (gpio-poweroff), reported; with poweroff-exit=on
              the rising line shuts QEMU down like the PMIC would.
  WIFI-RESET  GPIO1_IO04, the Broadcom module's reset.
  HALL-ENABLE GPIO7_IO02, the wheel's Hall power (also feeds the ADC's
              gate line, through a split irq).
  VBATT-EN    GPIO6_IO16, the battery divider's enable (likewise).

Every change goes out as "NAME in|out 0|1000 <guest-us>" — the machine
wires the banks in flintstone_init and exposes /machine/wheel-position
so the UI reaches the wheel at a stable QOM path.
